# Snake

See [custom applications](/docs/applications/custom/). This is a **Datastar +
Rocci stress demo**, not a second walkthrough and not a recommended game
architecture.

The point is to push a long-lived HTML morph stream: one authoritative 100×100
world, up to eight snakes, and ~8 Hz SSE patches of `#board`, `#hud`, and
`#minimap`. The HUD reports live bandwidth for that stream (rate, last patch,
total, patch count) so you can see what Datastar is actually moving. Keyboard
and touch steering stay in a tiny `snake-input.js` island; the world does not.

Lobby and board live in `Snake.rocci`, ticks and collisions in `Game.roc`, HTTP
and SSE in `main.roc`. This is **docs-only** on the public origin (not a live
hostname).

Each player’s camera stays put while the head moves inside the 31×21 view and
only scrolls when the head enters a three-cell margin. Spectators still track
the living-snake centroid. The minimap is the whole 100×100 world, so every
living snake stays visible even when it is off-camera.

## Run locally

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/custom/snake
```

If you already ran an older build, delete `examples/rocci/custom/snake/snake.db`
so the world schema can be created fresh.

## Smoke

```sh
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/ | grep -E 'Join game|Spectate'
```
